  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-05T19:37:52.496Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I can't speak for in-game performance, but in editor having OnGUI registered to every UdonBehaviour makes up a majority of the runtime overhead of empty behaviours. If I have 2000 UdonBehaviours in the scene with the Empty graph behaviour, it takes approximately 20ms on the CPU. Around 18.5ms of that overhead is from OnGUI. OnGUI also generates 0.7MB of garbage per frame for all of those events. Also note that OnGUI can run multiple times per behaviour.\n\nUdon doesn't currently expose any IMGUI functions as far as I can see, so there isn't really a point in registering the OnGUI event in the first place.",
